{"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Over 12 years I’ve built up a stack that I’m genuinely comfortable with,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not just familiar with. Here’s what I use and what I think of each."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Core Languages","anchor":"Core-Languages"},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Swift","anchor":"Swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"My primary language. I’ve been writing Swift since the early days and have","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"watched it mature into one of the best-designed languages in the industry.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Strong opinions on value types, protocol-oriented design, and the right","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"use of generics.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Objective-C","anchor":"Objective-C"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Still fluent. Legacy codebases don’t scare me — bridging Swift and ObjC"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in mixed projects is something I’ve done extensively."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"iOS Frameworks","anchor":"iOS-Frameworks"},{"type":"table","header":"row","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Framework"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Depth","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"UIKit","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Expert — built complex custom UI, animations, layout systems","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"SwiftUI"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Produc